","label":"Science","sourceId":"source-google-books-the-chemical-philosophy-paracelsian-science-and-medicine-in-the-sixteenth-and-seventeenth-centur"}],"pageCount":660,"summary":"Swiss-born physician and alchemist Paracelsus (1493–1541) and his disciples espoused a doctrine they proclaimed as a truly Christian interpretation of nature in chemistry. Drawing upon a mixture of ancient, medieval, and Renaissance sources, they developed a new philosophy that interpreted both macrocosmic and microcosmic events through the personal observations of the chemist and the Divine Grace of the Lord. Until the publication of this book, however, the breadth and vicissitudes of the Paracelsian approach to nature and medicine had been little studied. This volume spans more than a century, providing a rich record of the major interests of the Paracelsian and other chemical philosophers and the conflicts in which they engaged with their contemporaries.","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-the-chemical-philosophy-paracelsian-science-and-medicine-in-the-sixteenth-and-seventeenth-centur.jpg","displaySummary":"This volume spans more than a century, providing a rich record of the major interests of the Paracelsian and other chemical philosophers and the conflicts in which they engaged with their contemporaries.","primarySubject":"Science","primaryTopic":"Science & Discovery","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Science","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Science","score":6,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","rawLabel":"Science","mappedSubject":"Science","score":6,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-google-books-the-chemical-philosophy-paracelsian-science-and-medicine-in-the-sixteenth-and-seventeenth-centur","id":"subject-evidence-book-the-chemical-philosophy-paracelsian-science-and-medicine-in-the-sixteenth-and-seventeenth-centur-1"},{"source":"keyword_classifier","rawLabel":"Medicine & Public Hea